WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.584 --> 00:00:02.711
People instinctively
run from fire.

00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:04.046
So, we burn them out!

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:05.797
And if we burn down
the palace in the process?

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.382
We'll build a new one, Orlo.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:09.092
New palace, new Russia.

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:10.427
This-- this is madness.

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:12.179
These are some of the best sets
we've ever seen,

00:00:12.221 --> 00:00:14.598
and I... it's true.
I'm not biased.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.558
♪♪

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.144
TONY McNAMARA: This year,
we wanted the palace to change

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:20.687
because Catherine could change.

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:22.481
We wanted
the costumes to change,

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:24.608
because she was older
and had a stronger look.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.777
MARIAN MACGOWAN:
All of our designers
in Season 2,

00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:29.446
worked beautifully
in developing our world.

00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:32.699
The visual look is like period
show with an edge to it.

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:36.703
And that should be reflected
in design and costumes.

00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:37.788
Exactly!

00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.624
Visually, it was spectacular
and really fun.

00:00:40.666 --> 00:00:42.167
Look where we are.

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:44.086
We have built so many sets.

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:47.339
My passion is really to create
spaces from scratch.

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:50.050
I think that's what
really excites me
in the design process.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:53.720
Girls, go and stand over there
and... stare at art!

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:57.057
TONY: In terms of wardrobe,
and hair and makeup, and set

00:00:57.099 --> 00:00:59.017
inspiring us to how we write,

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.978
I have a very good,
strong dialogue

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:03.397
with those departments
all the time.

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:05.607
The design process
is always sort of

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:07.776
responding to what
the script needs.

00:01:07.818 --> 00:01:09.194
I am doing something here

00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:11.029
that will change the world.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.407
We did want the look

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:15.367
and the feel
of the palace interiors

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:17.786
to feel like they are grounded
in the 17th Century,

00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:20.372
but not a specific palace.

00:01:20.414 --> 00:01:24.209
We were liberated by not
being historically accurate.

00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:27.379
That allowed us to push
a design a little bit further.

00:01:27.421 --> 00:01:29.756
This is the Russia we create.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.968
The nursery's great 'cause
Peter sort of designed it.

00:01:33.302 --> 00:01:35.262
Ah! What color do you think?

00:01:35.304 --> 00:01:36.597
Not sure.

00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:38.140
I say each wall different.

00:01:38.182 --> 00:01:41.101
It had been Peter's nursery,
once upon a time.

00:01:41.143 --> 00:01:42.436
Look at that fireplace.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.396
TONY: So it has
this amazing fireplace

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:46.315
that is terrifying to children.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:49.234
He still has that slightly
off-kilter sense of him

00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:50.944
in that he can't
quite understand

00:01:50.986 --> 00:01:53.405
maybe what a child
should be witness to.

00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:55.657
I made this for Paul using parts
from real bears.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:00.412
Our costumes are so extravagant
and beautiful.

00:02:00.454 --> 00:02:02.456
What am I wearing?
Why am I wearing this?

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:03.749
I can't be wearing this!

00:02:04.041 --> 00:02:06.418
It's quite difficult
to do that century

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.253
without going overboard.

00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:10.839
With costumes, we were always
looking for opportunities

00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:13.842
where we can sort of
do something a bit absurd.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.013
-Velcro.
-Love it.

00:02:18.305 --> 00:02:20.599
SHARON:
Catherine the Great
was so clever,

00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:21.892
she used clothes as a tool.

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.310
ELLE:
In order to get done what

00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:25.229
she needed to do, politically.

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.481
-Ambassador Sunduk.
-Empress.

00:02:27.523 --> 00:02:29.233
Because she's become an empress,

00:02:29.274 --> 00:02:30.943
I tried to use bigger patterns.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.861
She's in charge, so...

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:35.948
she has to assert herself,
kind of, sharp lines.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:38.825
I think he found a loophole.
And a hat.

00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:41.286
Favorite costume, hands down,
the baby shower

00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:44.122
costume is Peter really wanting
to be the belle of the ball.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.959
And so it's got this
extravagant baby-colored

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.252
blues, pinks, yellows.

00:02:48.293 --> 00:02:50.003
Feather hat with big feathers

00:02:50.045 --> 00:02:51.129
and plumes and a dress.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.631
-Huzzah!
-(cheering)

00:02:52.673 --> 00:02:54.591
-Huzz-- ah.
-Beat you to it.

00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:56.635
I think, probably
my favorite costume
I've ever worn.

00:02:57.511 --> 00:02:59.012
I'm gonna say it. I did it.

00:02:59.555 --> 00:03:00.806
It's quite over the top.

00:03:00.848 --> 00:03:02.891
You liked what I wore
at the coronation?

00:03:02.933 --> 00:03:04.434
You looked stunning.

00:03:05.102 --> 00:03:07.688
ELLE: My favorite costume
was the coronation gown.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.857
It looked--
I was like, this looks like...

00:03:09.898 --> 00:03:11.817
you know, like, Gucci couture
or something.

00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:14.027
Like unreal.
This is like straight off a runway.

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:15.946
PETER: I've actually banned
most of those fabrics.

00:03:15.988 --> 00:03:17.447
I thought you were taking
Russia into the future,

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:19.867
-not into grandmother's house.
-Shut up.

00:03:19.908 --> 00:03:22.828
All those costumes,
they're just fun to be in,
they're fun to wear.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:23.996
Let us celebrate.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.330
SHARON:
It just all came together

00:03:25.372 --> 00:03:26.874
and it was lovely
and it was fun.

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:28.500
FRANCESCA:
It's a dream job because

00:03:28.542 --> 00:03:30.502
it's been an amazing
show to design.

00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:31.753
It doesn't matter how I look.

00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:33.130
Just what I do.

00:03:33.172 --> 00:03:34.381
(laughter)

00:03:34.423 --> 00:03:35.757
If you dress well,

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:38.468
no one notices what you do.
Just what you wear.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.345
♪ ♪

